msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:147
#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:156
msgid "Product analytics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:148
msgid "Sends page views and the interactions you choose to ZipLogger as product-analytics events, and exposes a small JavaScript API for your own events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:149
msgid "Event name, page path (no query string), timestamp, a random anonymous visitor id and a random session id. Nothing else is read from the page: not text, not form values, not every click. With \"identify\" on, logged-in users also get an opaque keyed hash of their WordPress user id - never an email address or username."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:150
msgid "Small batches sent from the browser while the visitor browses, and when the page is hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:151
msgid "Each event counts toward your ZipLogger event allowance. The visitor id is kept in your visitors' browser storage (localStorage) once the analytics consent policy allows it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:157
msgid "Send analytics events to ZipLogger"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:162
msgid "Page views"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:163
msgid "Send an event when a page is viewed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:168
msgid "Client-side navigation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:169
msgid "Also count page changes made without a reload (History API)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:174
msgid "Interaction events"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:175
msgid "Track clicks on the elements listed below and on elements with a data-ziplogger-event attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:180
msgid "Tracked elements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:182
msgid "One CSS selector per line (up to 20). Only clicks on a matching element are tracked; the event carries the selector, never the element's text or values. Give an element data-ziplogger-event=\"name\" to name the event yourself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:187
msgid "Identify logged-in users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:188
msgid "Link a signed-in user's events with a pseudonymous id (a keyed hash, not their email or username)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:193
#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:225
#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:320
msgid "Sampling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:197
msgid "Share of visitor sessions that send analytics. 100 tracks everyone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:210
#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:219
#: includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:49
#: includes/admin/tabs/class-privacy.php:37
#: includes/admin/tabs/class-privacy.php:59
msgid "Session replay"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:211
msgid "Records a sample of visitor sessions with ZipLogger's official replay recorder so you can watch what happened before an error. It is separate from every other module and off until you switch it on here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:212
msgid "A recording of the page as the visitor sees it: structure, clicks, scrolling and typing activity. All input values are masked and this cannot be turned off; password and payment fields are never recorded. By default all text is masked too. WordPress admin, login, account, cart, checkout and payment pages are never recorded, and you can add more exclusions. Cross-origin iframes (for example payment card fields hosted by your payment provider) cannot be recorded by any browser-side tool."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:213
msgid "The recorder script (about 23 KB compressed, measured at build time) is downloaded only for sessions that are sampled in, consented and on an eligible page. Recordings upload in compressed chunks every few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:214
msgid "Replay is metered separately in ZipLogger (sessions and stored bytes). The limits below cap one session's length and size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:220
msgid "Record sampled sessions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:229
msgid "Share of sessions recorded, decided once per session."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:234
msgid "Mask all text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:235
msgid "Replace all text on the page with placeholder characters in the recording (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:236
msgid "Turn this off only if every page you record shows public content. Input values stay masked either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:241
msgid "Additionally mask"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:243
msgid "CSS selectors (one per line) whose text is masked. Elements with data-ziplogger-mask are always masked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:248
msgid "Block completely"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:250
msgid "CSS selectors (one per line) that are replaced by an empty box. Elements with data-ziplogger-ignore are always blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:255
msgid "Never record these pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:257
msgid "URL paths starting with \"/\" (one per line, * matches anything). Added to the built-in exclusions, which cannot be removed: wp-admin, login, registration, password reset, my account, cart, checkout, order pay and order received."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:262
msgid "Never record users with these roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:263
msgid "Logged-in users holding any of these roles are not recorded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:268
msgid "Longest recording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:269
msgid "minutes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:276
msgid "Largest recording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:280
msgid "Uncompressed size after which a session stops recording."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:293
msgid "Distributed tracing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:294
msgid "Records how long WordPress takes to answer requests, and the outbound HTTP calls it makes while doing so, as OpenTelemetry traces in ZipLogger. Requests that already carry a trace context from the browser are joined to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:295
msgid "For a sampled request: method, a route template (for example \"single\" or \"/wc/v3/orders/(?P<id>)\"), response status, duration, the WordPress request type (front end, admin, REST, AJAX, cron) and a count of database queries. For outbound calls: host, method, status and duration - never the path or query string. The URL path of your own pages is added only if you switch that on below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:296
msgid "Spans are queued locally and sent by the same background job as logs. The trace header is added to outbound requests only for the hosts you list below, never to other third parties."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:297
msgid "Spans share your ZipLogger ingest volume with logs. Sampling controls how many requests produce a trace; the local queue keeps at most half of its capacity for spans."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:302
#: includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:50
#: includes/admin/tabs/class-privacy.php:38
msgid "Tracing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:303
msgid "Send traces to ZipLogger"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:308
msgid "Request spans"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:309
msgid "One span per sampled WordPress request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:314
msgid "Outbound calls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:315
msgid "A child span for each outbound wp_remote_*() call in a sampled request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:324
msgid "Share of requests that start a new trace. A request that arrives with a trace context follows the caller's sampling decision instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:329
msgid "Send trace headers to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:331
msgid "Host names (one per line) that receive a W3C traceparent header on outbound requests. Empty means none. Only traceparent is sent, never baggage or cookies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:336
msgid "Service name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:338
msgid "How this site appears in ZipLogger traces. Defaults to the site label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:343
msgid "URL path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:344
msgid "Also record the request path (no query string)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:345
msgid "Paths can contain personal data such as member slugs. Off by default; the route template is always recorded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:350
msgid "Database query count"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:351
msgid "Record how many queries WordPress ran (free: read from the database class, nothing is measured)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:356
msgid "Database timing (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:357
msgid "On sampled requests only, also measure total query time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:358
msgid "Uses WordPress's query log on sampled requests, which has a real cost: it keeps every query in memory. Covers queries made through $wpdb after this plugin loads; earlier queries and direct database connections are not covered. Query text is never recorded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:363
msgid "Browser to server"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:364
msgid "Trace this site's own fetch/XHR calls in the browser and link them to the server request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-module-specs.php:365
msgid "Adds a traceparent header to same-site requests (WordPress AJAX, REST, WooCommerce Store API). Spans are sent from the browser with the browser key. Page-load requests are not linked, because pages may be cached and must not contain a trace id."
msgstr ""

